WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.090
Every engineer knows this pile.

00:02.264 --> 00:06.722
A vacuum breaker manual, hundreds of pages, and a transformer standard written in

00:06.757 --> 00:08.104
the language of committees.

00:08.615 --> 00:11.633
The Siemens book is worse than dense — it's a scan.

00:11.842 --> 00:14.292
No selectable text, nothing you can search.

00:14.570 --> 00:17.136
You squint at a page and cross-reference a legend.

00:17.647 --> 00:21.455
Spec Explorer takes those two documents and makes them something you can actually

00:21.548 --> 00:21.800
use.

00:21.800 --> 00:24.819
So here's the first thing you can do — just ask it, in plain

00:24.877 --> 00:25.677
English.

00:25.724 --> 00:28.151
How do I manually charge the closing spring?

00:28.661 --> 00:32.714
Behind the scenes, that Siemens manual was a scan — no searchable text at

00:32.772 --> 00:37.125
all — so it was read by OCR, character by character, just to recover

00:37.160 --> 00:37.960
the words.

00:38.286 --> 00:41.781
Now the answer comes straight from that text, and only that text.

00:42.292 --> 00:43.499
No invented numbers.

00:43.673 --> 00:46.332
And it cites the page it came from, so you can go and check

00:46.367 --> 00:47.342
it yourself.

00:47.342 --> 00:49.327
Now, the diagram explorer.

00:49.710 --> 00:55.074
This is Figure 15 — the stored energy operating mechanism — a scanned photograph

00:55.225 --> 00:57.234
with three dozen numbered callouts.

00:57.675 --> 00:59.173
Every one of them is clickable.

00:59.684 --> 01:03.736
Click sixty-two, and the panel tells you: that's the closing spring, and what it

01:03.782 --> 01:04.582
does.

01:04.676 --> 01:08.333
The legend you used to hunt through is right there under your cursor.

01:08.342 --> 01:12.568
Back in the explorer, open Figure 17 — the operating sequence.

01:13.009 --> 01:17.154
How the breaker closes, and how it trips, drawn as a flowchart of cryptic

01:17.212 --> 01:18.234
device codes.

01:18.838 --> 01:23.249
Click a step — the shunt trip coil, fifty-two T — and it decodes

01:23.296 --> 01:25.014
the shorthand into plain English.

01:25.525 --> 01:28.079
Every box in the diagram, translated.

01:28.079 --> 01:31.632
Two documents that used to mean squinting and cross-referencing.

01:32.235 --> 01:35.556
Now you ask them a question, and you explore them by hand.

01:35.997 --> 01:40.432
It's live, at spec-explorer-esr.netlify.app.
